    "title": "Waco ISD Teacher Raises Hundreds in 3 Days to Buy Classroom Materials - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Robert Lopez ,\n6 hours ago\nWACO, Texas ( FOX 44 ) – Waco Independent School District seventh-grade math teacher Mary Evans raised over $600 to buy materials for her math class.\nWhen Evans started her fundraiser on Donors Choose , she didn’t expect that she would raise all $613 of it as fast as she did. She submitted the project on September 13th; it was approved and posted on the 14th and was fully funded before the end the day on the 15th.\n“I decided to just donate myself into it,” said Ms. Evans. “I donated $25, and I made the post. I said, ‘Can someone just help match me so I can meet my goal?’ Went to bed that night and the next morning it was fully funded.”\nG. W. Carver Principal Dennise Wooden says Evans’ latest fundraising effort is the latest in a long-running series of philanthropic activities she’s done for the school.\n“How ever she can get community involvement to come into the school and help those kids learn. That’s 100 percent what she’s there for,” said Wooden. “They do whatever they have to do like bring any supplies, deodorant. They’ve done toiletry bags for the kids. Anything that the kids need so that they have what they need to learn.”\nG. W. Carver Middle School serves a 96.3 percent economically-disadvantaged student body. With this comes challenges that other middle schools don’t have to face. The actions taken by Evans and others in the community are an effort to make G.W. Carver a safe space for the students.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KWKT - FOX 44.\n3",
